Chapter: TraceStackProbe
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Asks the stack high-water cell directly. The boot prologue seeds
 stack-min-rsp-addr (28736) with ram-size unconditionally, and only a
 trace-alloc build emits the per-prologue store that narrows it. So a plain
 build must report narrowed=0 and a trace build must report narrowed=1: the
 same source, the same kernel, the switch the only difference.

 deep recurses non-tail so the frames are real and RSP genuinely descends.

Section: Definitions

  deep : Integer -> Integer
  deep (n) =
   if n <= 0 then 0
   else 1 + deep (n - 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   d <- print-line-uni ("depth: " & show (deep 200))
   let ram = peek-qword 4072 0
   in let hwm = peek-qword 28736 0
   in act
    print-line-uni ("narrowed: " & show (if hwm < ram then 1 else 0))
   end
  end
